schneck@math.berkeley.edu wrote:
> I see that I misunderstood Hearse.  I always imagined that all the
> Hearse users had entirely independent access to a vast and ever-growing
> bones collection.  Instead (and doubtless more sensibly) it's closer a
> normal multiplayer setup, in that once someone downloads a bones file,
> it's gone for everyone else.

It's sort of a middle ground.  If there are more than 1000 bones 
available for that particular version, then a bones file can only be 
downloaded by one user before it's expired from the server.  Otherwise, 
two users are allowed to downloaded it.

Basically the server tries to keep a healthy supply of bones files for 
any given version, the number 1000 being chosen entirely arbitrarily.

It does mean that bones files don't hang around forever - which is just 
as well since over 18,000 bones files have been uploaded to Hearse since 
it started!

